It depends on the version, because the published docs and the current source on GitHub don't agree. (Ludion had no lessons on this, so I checked the docs and the source myself.)

**What the published docs say** ([Queue tasks reference](https://developers.cloudflare.com/agents/api-reference/queue-tasks/)):
- `getQueue` is synchronous: `getQueue<T>(id: string): QueueItem<T> | undefined`
- `QueueItem` has these fields:
  ```ts
  type QueueItem<T> = {
    id: string;            // unique task ID
    payload: T;            // data passed to the callback
    callback: keyof Agent; // name of the method to call
    created_at: number;    // creation timestamp
    retry?: RetryOptions;  // retry options
  };
  ```

**What the current `main` branch says** (`packages/agents/src/index.ts`, `src/queue/types.ts`):
- `getQueue` is not marked `async`, but it returns a Promise:
  ```ts
  getQueue<T = unknown>(id: string): Promise<QueueItem<T> | undefined>
  ```
  It hands the work to `this._queue.get(id)`.
- `QueueItem` uses camelCase and a looser `callback` type:
  ```ts
  export type QueueItem<T = unknown> = {
    id: string;
    callback: string;
    payload: T;
    createdAt: number;
    retry?: RetryOptions;
  };
  ```

**What to do:** Use `await this.getQueue(id)`. On the synchronous version, awaiting a plain value does no harm. On the Promise version, leaving out `await` gives you a Promise instead of the item. Before you rely on `created_at` or `createdAt`, check `node_modules/agents/dist/*.d.ts` for your installed version. I didn't confirm which npm release made the change, and `main` may include changes that haven't been released yet.

Sources:
- https://developers.cloudflare.com/agents/api-reference/queue-tasks/
- https://github.com/cloudflare/agents/blob/main/packages/agents/src/index.ts
- https://github.com/cloudflare/agents/blob/main/packages/agents/src/queue/types.ts

